          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Pierre\",\"addressee\":\"Hélène\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Je vous aime!\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The focal expression directly presents Pierre's love for Hélène as true. His preceding inner formulation also frames it as a belief about his own state, regardless of the scene's doubts about depth or sincerity.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"«Теперь уж поздно, всё кончено; да и я люблю ее», подумал Пьер.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.86,\"reason\":\"The words occur after Pierre and Hélène have publicly been treated as engaged and while Pierre holds the hand of his fiancée. Pierre understands that a conventional statement required by this occasion remains to be made. Thus this occurrence does more than report emotion: it substantially ratifies his acceptance of Hélène as his fiancée and affirms the marital bond into which the gathering has positioned them. It does not clearly constitute a separate, explicit proposal or specify obligations, so undertaking force is substantial rather than dominant.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Пьер молча держал руку своей невесты\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"«Что-то такое особенное говорят в этих случаях», думал он, но никак не мог вспомнить, чтò такое именно говорят в этих случаях.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"сказал он, вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.96,\"reason\":\"Although punctuated as an exclamation, the expression is not represented as a reflexive outburst or affective discharge. Pierre deliberately recalls and supplies the conventional words expected in the situation, and then judges their delivery inadequate.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"сказал он, вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях; но слова эти прозвучали так бедно, что ему стало стыдно за себя.\"},{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.91,\"reason\":\"No additional core force needs to be posited. The direct avowal is captured by T, while its contextual function as a conventional ratification of the engagement is captured by P.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"Pierre and Hélène are alone after their assembled relatives have already congratulated and blessed them as an engaged couple. Pierre, embarrassed and under strong social pressure, holds his fiancée's hand, searches for the words conventionally expected on such an occasion, and tells her that he loves her.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"mixed\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The focal expression substantially affirms Pierre's acceptance of the socially established engagement and his position as Hélène's future husband; it ratifies rather than clearly initiates the undertaking. Hélène has already moved closer and initiated a kiss, while the family has already treated the engagement as settled. No verbal response from her after the focal words is supplied. The passage later states that they married, which establishes the eventual outcome but does not by itself determine the immediate uptake or sincerity of this utterance.\",\"recognised_work\":true,\"recognition_note\":\"Recognised as a passage from Leo Tolstoy's War and Peace; the classification relies only on the supplied evidence.\",\"limitations\":\"The supplied scene shows attraction and Pierre's inner thought that he loves Hélène, but also fear, shame, ambivalence, and intense social orchestration, so the quality and sincerity of his affection remain mixed. It does not provide Hélène's response after the focal utterance or explicit negotiated terms of the engagement.\"}"
        }
